# Stack conventions

## Pinned stack

Production host is Vercel + Supabase + R2 + Resend + Inngest + Upstash. Sentry is optional. The full secret inventory is the contract in `.env.example` and `docs/architecture.md`. Production boot (`src/lib/env.ts`) throws if a required secret is missing. Development fallbacks (local disk, skip mail, in-process jobs, in-memory rate limit, `AUTH_DEV_BYPASS`) stay development only.

- **App:** Next.js 16 App Router + React 19 + TypeScript (`src/`)
- **DB:** PostgreSQL via Supabase; Prisma 7 with `@prisma/adapter-pg`
- **Auth:** Supabase Auth only — never NextAuth / Auth.js. Use `src/proxy.ts` (Next 16; not middleware) to gate `/admin/*`.
- **Storage:** Cloudflare R2 via S3-compatible API (zero egress)
- **PDFs:** `pdf-lib` overlay rendering + `qrcode` package
- **Designer:** Fabric.js — layout JSON, not HTML-to-PDF
- **Jobs:** Inngest for bulk CSV + email
- **Email:** Resend (Phase 0) or SES at higher volume
- **Rate limit:** Upstash Ratelimit on public `/v/*` (fail closed in production)
- **Host:** Vercel (app) + Supabase (DB/Auth) + R2 (files)
- **Runtime:** Node.js ≥ 24

## Project layout

- `src/app/(public)/` — landing, `/v/[id]`, login
- `src/app/(admin)/admin/` — club admin dashboard
- `src/lib/certificates/` — HMAC token, ID, verify decision
- `src/lib/auth.ts` · `src/lib/audit.ts` · `src/proxy.ts`
- `src/lib/supabase/` — browser + server clients
- `prisma/schema.prisma` + `prisma7.config.ts`
- `supabase/rls-policies.sql` then `supabase/app-role.sql` — apply after migrate. Runtime `DATABASE_URL` is `leoverify_app`; migrate uses `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL`.

## Prisma 7 notes

- Import client from `@/generated/prisma/client`
- Always pass a driver adapter: `new PrismaClient({ adapter })`
- Datasource URL lives in `prisma7.config.ts`, not `schema.prisma`
- Run `npx prisma generate` after schema changes

## Do not

- Commit `.env` or real secrets
- Add blockchain / exotic crypto for Phase 0/1
- Put login walls on `/v/*`
- Use Puppeteer for certificate rendering (overlay approach only)
